{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (NURSE): Mr. Krishnan, blood pressure today is one oh nine over seventy-seven. Sorry, I nearly wrote one nineteen, it is one oh nine over seventy-seven.",
  "[SEG0002] person_1 (NURSE): Pulse seventy-six. Temperature is thirty-eight point three degrees. Weight today is fifty-two kilograms.",
  "[SEG0003] person_1 (NURSE): Last time in March you were sixty-eight. Your last pressure was one-forty.",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (PATIENT): Sixty-eight? That was all the ladoos at my cousin's wedding, three days of eating. Now the trousers are hanging only.",
  "[SEG0005] person_3 (DOCTOR): Come, sit, Mr. Krishnan. What has been troubling you these days?",
  "[SEG0006] person_2 (PATIENT): Night time I am getting up to pass urine, doctor. Three times, sometimes four. The stream is weak, and it dribbles at the end.",
  "[SEG0007] person_2 (PATIENT): And that neighbour's dog starts barking the moment I get up, so sleep is gone. Useless animal.",
  "[SEG0008] person_3 (DOCTOR): Mm. Since when has the getting up at night been there?",
  "[SEG0009] person_2 (PATIENT): Umm, I cannot say the date. Some months, I think. Not from yesterday only.",
  "[SEG0010] person_4 (CAREGIVER): Madam, I am the carer, I stay in the house. I hear him get up three to four times every night. Same as he is saying.",
  "[SEG0011] person_3 (DOCTOR): Of. Is the flow slow right from the start?",
  "[SEG0012] person_2 (PATIENT): Yes, weak only. I stand and stand, then a little dribbling on the underwear. Even at the tea stall I have to rush, very embarrassing.",
  "[SEG0013] person_3 (DOCTOR): Any blood in the urine?",
  "[SEG0014] person_2 (PATIENT): No no, nothing like blood. Colour is normal.",
  "[SEG0015] person_3 (DOCTOR): Any burning or pain when you pass urine?",
  "[SEG0016] person_2 (PATIENT): No burning. Pain also no.",
  "[SEG0017] person_3 (DOCTOR): Do you take tea in the evening?",
  "[SEG0018] person_2 (PATIENT): Tea I cannot leave. Two cups after six, sometimes three if the serial is boring. My late wife used to scold me for it, what to do.",
  "[SEG0019] person_3 (DOCTOR): Tell me the tablets you are on now.",
  "[SEG0020] person_2 (PATIENT): For the pressure, Mizartan forty milligram in the morning. For sugar, Metformine five hundred milligram, morning and night. Omprazole twenty milligram before food for the acidity. Err, and the water tablet, the small white one, when my feet swell.",
  "[SEG0021] person_2 (PATIENT): Crocin I stopped. Knee was paining last winter, now it is okay, so I left it.",
  "[SEG0022] person_4 (CAREGIVER): Doctor, the evening Metformine he forgets. 2, 3 days in a week he skips. I keep the strip on the table only.",
  "[SEG0023] person_3 (DOCTOR): Any allergy to a medicine?",
  "[SEG0024] person_2 (PATIENT): No, nothing. All tablets suit me.",
  "[SEG0025] person_3 (DOCTOR): How about the bowels, any problem there?",
  "[SEG0026] person_2 (PATIENT): Motions are fine. Daily. No loose motion.",
  "[SEG0027] person_3 (DOCTOR): Right. Your sugar and your pressure are ongoing, we know that. The weak stream and the night waking, I think this is most likely the prostate, a benign enlargement, though not confirmed until the tests.",
  "[SEG0028] person_3 (DOCTOR): Temperature is a little raised, thirty-eight point three, so I will arrange a urine test to look for infection, and a PSA blood test. I am also starting tamsulosin, zero point four milligram, one tablet at night for the stream.",
  "[SEG0029] person_2 (PATIENT): Tamsu-what? My brother in law took a prostate tablet and got dizzy in the temple queue. I don't want all that drama, doctor.",
  "[SEG0030] person_3 (DOCTOR): It can make some people dizzy on standing, so get up slowly. Kindly cut the evening tea to one cup. We will see you back in three weeks with the reports.",
  "[SEG0031] person_4 (CAREGIVER): I will bring him, madam. And I will watch the evening tablet.",
  "[SEG0032] person_2 (PATIENT): Three weeks is fine, though the auto fare has become mad. Okay okay, we will come."
 ],
